IMO it's _much_ more fun to play on NAO than locally, because:
a) you can track your stats and rankings
b) you get lots of interesting bones (Hearse helps here for local
games)
c) Other people can watch you play (and give advice if you hang out on
IRC; and
d) you get ttyrecs to go back and watch.
e) You get to play in the tournament (and the experience preps you for
the devnull tourney too)

NAO is a telnet interface.  Even if you want to play locally now, I'd
recommend not using tiles so that the shift to NAO (or the devnull
tournament) isn't a shock later.


